# Whisper-wave Client — Cursor AI Rules

Condensed mirror of `CLAUDE.md` (the full source of truth — read it for detail and
examples). These rules are non-negotiable. When in doubt, extract to the correct
layer rather than keeping code in a component. Keep this file in sync with
`CLAUDE.md`: if one changes, change both in the same commit.

---

## 1. Architecture — Feature-Sliced, One-Way Dependencies

Layers and the ONLY allowed dependency direction:

```
pages  ──▶  features  ──▶  shared
             (features may use shared; shared must NEVER import features)
```

```
src/
  app/            router.tsx, providers.tsx, queryClient.ts, RouteError.tsx  (wiring only)
  pages/          thin route entries — compose features, no business logic
  layout/         AppWrapper, AdminWrapper
  features/<domain>/    auth · chat · admin · profile · notifications · landing
      api/        axios calls (no logic/UI)
      components/  hooks/  stores/  utils/
      types.ts    ALL domain data-model types
      index.ts    PUBLIC API — the only thing other slices may import
  shared/         domain-agnostic ONLY
      components/  (ui/ icons/ charts/ skeletons/ media/ image-viewer/ sidebar/ tables/)
      hooks/  utils/  constants/
      lib/         api/client.ts (axios), socket/ (SocketProvider)
      types/       user.ts, icon.ts, media.ts, socket.ts, ui.ts, index.ts (barrel)
  assets/  styles/  main.tsx
```

- No other top-level folders under `src/`. No feature code in `pages/`/`app/`/`layout/`.
- **`shared/` importing `@/features/...` is the #1 forbidden smell.** Move the file
  into the owning feature instead.
- Cross-feature use goes through `@/features/<domain>` (its `index.ts`) only — never
  deep subpaths. Inside a feature, use relative imports.

---

## 2. Separation of Concerns

Components render JSX. Hooks decide. Utils compute (pure, no side effects). Api
fetches. Stores hold state.

| Concern           | Where                                       |
|-------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Data fetching     | `hooks/useXxxQueries.ts` (TanStack Query)   |
| Mutations         | `hooks/useXxxMutations.ts`                  |
| Derived UI logic  | `hooks/useXxx.ts`                           |
| Pure transforms   | `utils/…` (no toast/navigate/network/hooks) |
| HTTP calls        | `features/<domain>/api/…`                   |
| Global client state | `stores/…` (zustand)                      |

No data fetching, `.then()` chains, or business logic inside a component body.
Extract to a hook.

---

## 3. Modern Stack — Use It the Current Way

React 19 · TS (strict) · Vite 8 · Tailwind v4 · TanStack Query v5 · Zustand v5 ·
react-hook-form v7 + Zod v4 · react-router v7 · socket.io-client v4 · dayjs.

- Server data → TanStack Query. **Never** `useState`+`useEffect`+fetch.
- Client/UI/session state → Zustand (selectors; no server data inside).
- Forms → react-hook-form + Zod (`z.infer` for the type; schema is source of truth).
- `useEffect` only to sync with external systems (DOM/socket/subscriptions), never
  to fetch; always clean up. Prefer derivation over mirrored state.
- Realtime → `useSocketEvent` + `shared/constants/socketEvents.ts`; handlers update
  the Query cache/stores, not local copies.
- Function components + hooks only. No class components, no deprecated APIs, no `any`.

---

## 4. Types & Interfaces — Strict Placement

- Only type in a `.tsx`: its own `type Props = {…}` above the component.
- A hook `.ts` may have one private `interface Params {…}`.
- Everything else: domain models → `features/<domain>/types.ts`; shared shapes →
  `shared/types/{ui,media,socket,user,icon}.ts`. Never export a reusable type from a
  component/hook file.

---

## 5. Quality Bar

- **≤ 350 lines/file.** Over → split into sub-components / focused hooks.
- No `console.*`, no commented-out code, no dead code, no unused exports.
- Accessibility required: semantic HTML, keyboard-usable controls, `aria-label` on
  icon buttons, `aria-hidden` on decorative SVGs, visible focus, honor
  `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Path alias `@/` for cross-layer imports; relative only within a feature/folder.
- Naming: Components PascalCase; hooks `useX`; utils camelCase; scalar constants
  SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE; folders kebab-case.
- Before "done": `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` must pass.

---

## 6. Adding Code

- **New feature** → `features/<domain>/` with `api/ components/ hooks/ stores/ utils/
  types.ts index.ts`; put types in `types.ts` up front; expose surface via `index.ts`;
  register route in `app/router.tsx` (lazy-load if heavy).
- **New shared component** → correct `shared/components/<category>/` folder; local
  `Props` type; stays domain-agnostic (data via props, never imports a feature).
